8 workers, 2s of work on average: capacity 4 requests a second. Callers give up after 6s.

               no deadline check            deadline checked first     
  arrivals/s            in time    wasted            in time    wasted
         3.2              3.12/s     0.11/s              3.08/s     0.06/s
         4.0              2.57/s     1.49/s              3.45/s     0.40/s
         4.8              0.19/s     4.65/s              3.17/s     0.80/s
         6.0              0.06/s     6.09/s              2.96/s     1.10/s
         8.0              0.06/s     7.79/s              2.81/s     1.29/s

At 2x capacity the unchecked server stayed fully busy and answered 0.06 requests a
second in time. Starting a request only when its caller would still be waiting after
typical work answered 2.81, from the same workers.
Throughput is what the server did. Goodput is what callers received, and past capacity
the two part company unless the server stops starting work nobody is waiting for.
